# Never send local/secret files into the Docker build context — the
# Dockerfile's `COPY . .` would otherwise copy them verbatim into the build
# stage. In particular, a repo-root .env with NODE_ENV=development gets
# picked up by ui/*/vite.config.ts (envDir: REPO_ROOT) and flips
# import.meta.env.PROD to false for those builds even though `vite build`
# is running, breaking anything gated on PROD instead of BASE_URL/command.
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
!env.example.txt

# Local toolchain state — must come from npm ci inside the image, not the
# host's (possibly macOS/arm64) node_modules with incompatible native
# binaries (esbuild, etc.)
node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.github

# Build outputs (regenerated by `npm run build` inside the image)
dist
build

# IDE/editor/OS cruft
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Logs and local scratch
*.log
.manus-logs
logs
tmp
temp

# Docs not needed at build/runtime
docs
*.md
